{
  "baseCommit": "09dce0381b612f392112b23de4f69780418fd856",
  "boundaries": [
    "Native cleanup derives authority from the exact original locked journal, retained generation and certified vote without external historical voting observations. It never returns an old application ACK.",
    "Stable-three EMPTY original process replay reconstructs public bootstrap, the first BARRIER certificate/applied ends and a higher-ballot carried selection. Twelve halt/SIGKILL cases use 24 fresh JVMs and six live lock probes; no power-loss claim.",
    "The independent reader derives complete retirement marker/file maps and force/delete order, unchanged pending certificate/selector and replay claims. Twelve exact negatives and normal/optimized/relocated results pass.",
    "Covered-prefix cleanup, volatile higher-ballot fencing and new-ballot continuation/publication are separate Java tests, not additional process-matrix profiles.",
    "Four native tests pass in the final continuation snapshot. Fourteen existing tests pass in the qualified snapshot with identical production Java; only the new continuation test source differs. Initial and intermediate failures remain retained.",
    "All 661 V5.3 Python tests pass normally and under optimization. Existing staged-handoff replay and fifteen negatives pass with its original conditional-bootstrap boundary; actual six-profile covered replay, 36 in-process interruptions and seventeen negatives also pass.",
    "No disk/wire/public API/resource/workflow change. Local unresolved future proof still pins its original end, and selection still refuses unresolved imports until complete proof ownership is implemented.",
    "Selected future transfer, quorum-gated real dispatch, automatic maintenance/offline-survivor continuation, learners/joint transitions and all remaining 3B\u20133E obligations remain required.",
    "No push, PR, cloud execution, public runtime enablement or V5.2 Runner change."
  ],
